From 8769e8c1b6052d1c8ef1c93280ea36212141fefd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: goumin <min.gou@spacemit.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 16:06:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 344/468] SPACEMIT: ufs: spacemit: enable WriteBooster
 capability

FROM: https://github.com/spacemit-com/linux-6.18/commit/00340be01b32288a0ef2564c1406dc9243a04b00

Advertise UFSHCD_CAP_WB_EN so the UFS core can enable WriteBooster
on supported devices with an already provisioned buffer.

The core checks device version, feature support, buffer allocation and
buffer lifetime before enabling WB. Devices without a configured WB
buffer continue to operate with WB disabled. Leave device provisioning
outside the host driver.

Validated automatic WB enablement on YMTC YMUS8B5TH1A1C1 and Kingston
TY7B-128 using the same K3 kernel, and fallback with unallocated buffers.

Change-Id: I08235d658d17aa99caf96f30869686d5355a08a6
Signed-off-by: goumin <min.gou@spacemit.com>

(cherry picked from commit 553483f88352a436f19d3cf2fd444128e634ec30)

Change-Id: I3662cbef9911d7ab7328437621848ee920740128
[Han Gao: our driver is the version posted upstream (v7), set UFSHCD_CAP_WB_EN in ufs_spacemit_init()]
Signed-off-by: Han Gao <gaohan@iscas.ac.cn>
---
 drivers/ufs/host/ufs-spacemit.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-spacemit.c b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-spacemit.c
index 65aeba393b0f8..1b7f48695d356 100644
--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-spacemit.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-spacemit.c
@@ -453,6 +453,7 @@ static int ufs_spacemit_init(struct ufs_hba *hba)
 	ufs_spacemit_advertise_quirks(hba);
 
 	hba->caps |= UFSHCD_CAP_RPM_AUTOSUSPEND;
+	hba->caps |= UFSHCD_CAP_WB_EN;
 
 	return 0;
 }
